      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Applicants now seek emergency relief from this Court, arguing that OSHA's mandate exceeds its statutory authority and is otherwise unlawful."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Covered employers must \u201cdevelop, implement, and enforce a mandatory COVID\u201319 vaccination policy.\u201d Id., at 61402."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "OSHA published its vaccine mandate on November 5, 2021."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0000-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Judge Sutton dissented, joined by seven of his colleagues."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And employers who commit violations face hefty fnes: up to $13,653 for a standard violation, and up to $136,532 for a willful one. 29 CFR \u00a7 1903.15(d) (2021)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Confrming the point, the Act's provisions typically speak to hazards that employees face at work. See, e. g., \u00a7\u00a7 651, 653, 657. And no provision of the Act addresses public health more generally, which falls outside of OSHA's sphere of expertise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Solicitor General does not dispute that OSHA is limited to regulating \u201cwork-related dangers.\u201d Response Brief for OSHA in No. 21A244 etc., p. 45 (OSHA Response). She instead argues that the risk of contracting COVID\u201319 qualifes as such a danger."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "* * * The applications for stays presented to Justice Kavanaugh and by him referred to the Court are granted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal Government",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0001-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For its part, the Federal Government says that the mandate will save over 6,500 lives and prevent hundreds of thousands of hospitalizations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0001-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Standard falls within the core of the agency's mission: to \u201cprotect employees\u201d from \u201cgrave danger\u201d that comes from \u201cnew hazards\u201d or exposure to harmful agents. 29 U. S. C. \u00a7 655(c)(1). OSHA estimates\u2014and there is no ground for disputing\u2014that the Standard will save over 6,500 lives and prevent over 250,000 hospitalizations in six months' time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "sion commands\u2014not just enables, but commands\u2014OSHA to issue an emergency temporary standard whenever it determines \u201c(A) that employees are exposed to grave danger from exposure to substances or agents determined to be toxic or physically harmful or from new hazards, and (B) that such emergency standard is necessary to protect employees from such danger.\u201d 29 U. S. C. \u00a7 655(c)(1)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21a244",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "797cd667f062a7e051d50682446c857399f07ff306ae972f72345c0721dc8fab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-797cd667f062-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "OSHA's determinations are \u201cconclusive if supported by substantial evidence.\u201d 29 U. S. C. \u00a7 655(f). Judicial review under that test is deferential, as it should be."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
